# Detail Page and Related List Pattern

Follow existing admin detail pages (e.g. patrons, turnouts). Do not invent a new layout.

## Layout and header

- `sf-card` sections; Basic Information uses `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3`
- Group related fields (e.g. Service & Mailing Address in one card)
- Labels `sf-field-label`, values `sf-field-value`
- Page title with Edit `Link` in the top right

## Field validation highlighting

Highlight the **field container**, not the card:

```tsx
<div className={(() => {
  const mismatch = Math.abs(expected - actual) > 0.01
  return mismatch ? 'sf-field-highlighted' : ''
})()}>
  <p className="sf-field-label">Field Name</p>
  <p className="sf-field-value">{value}</p>
</div>
```

## Related lists

- Wrap in `WindowShade` with `defaultOpen={false}` and `title={`Items (${items.length})`}`
- Put a "New Item" action on the shade (`sf-btn sf-btn-secondary text-xs`)
- Table: `sf-table`
- Names that have a detail page are `Link`s with `text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-900`
- Truncate long text (notes) to 100 chars + `...`

## Add-item modals

- New modal at `src/components/[Item]Modal.tsx`
- Props: `isOpen`, `onClose`, `parentId`, `onItemAdded`
- Buttons: `sf-btn sf-btn-primary` / `sf-btn sf-btn-secondary`
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer ${localStorage.getItem('token')}`
- On success: `onItemAdded()`, `onClose()`, reset form
- Parent page: modal state + refetch handler; render the modal at the bottom

## Creating related records from a detail page

Prefer a query param so the new-record form pre-fills the parent:

```tsx
<Link href={`/admin/items/new?parentId=${patron.id}`} className="sf-btn sf-btn-secondary text-xs">
  New Item
</Link>
```

On the new page, `useSearchParams()` + `useEffect` to set `parentId`.

## Foreign keys and APIs

- On related detail pages, the parent name links back when the API returns parent `id`
- Prisma `include` / `select` the parent id and display fields
- Mutations: `setCurrentUserId(user.userId, userName)` then `clearCurrentUserId()` (including on error)
